  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 756a5c2e7946b9444ace4d21f0c402f5, type: 3}
  m_Name: New Dialogue Data
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueData
  speakerName: 
  lines:
  - ....... ....... .......... ...........
  - 'Kneel, child of ash. You stand before a sovereign of the eternal firmament. '
  - "This husk of stars has waited long for a soul bold enough \u2014 or foolish
    enough \u2014 to seek my audience. "
  - 'Your kind calls this world ''home.'' I unmade a thousand such cradles before
    your sun ever burned. '
  - What do I look like....?
  - The Queen....? Do not mistake this for what I am, mortal. What I truly am would
    unmake the marrow of your eyes.
  - "What you see now is a courtesy \u2014 a shape your fragile mind can hold. A
    translation. Nothing more. "
  - Even now, my true form goes untranslated. There are no words in your tongue,
    nor any tongue of flesh, for what I am.
  - 'Strike, if you must. The stars themselves have struck me, and learned humility
    for it. '
  - 'Enough words. Let the dust speak, if it has anything left to say. '
